## Can you reuse it?

**Algorand:** I found no from-scratch requirement in its rules; it is explicitly about deploying and growing an endpoint over months.

**ETHGlobal:** existing WorkerKit code needs to be handled under a suitable **Continuity track** rather than pretending you wrote it during ETHOnline. ETHGlobal explicitly allows existing projects in Continuity tracks, provided you document the existing baseline and build substantive new functionality during the event. ([ETHGlobal][3])

So before ETHOnline:

```bash
git tag pre-ethonline-2026
```

Then the ETHOnline work can clearly be things like:

```text
NEW DURING ETHONLINE

x402 capability discovery
Hedera Blocky402 adapter
BUY vs BUILD planner
autonomous payment
payment-aware RunMeter
provider quality feedback
HCS payment/run audit trail
```

Very defensible.

